description:
File: rust/lichen-rpl/src/multi_instance.rs
Lines: 553-561

When processing a DAO backbone message with multiple targets and multiple transits, only the first transit is used for all targets:

```rust
for target in message.targets {
    let transit = message.transit.first().cloned().unwrap_or(DaoTransit {
        path_sequence: message.dao_sequence,
        path_lifetime: 60,
        path_control: 0,
        parent: None,
    });
    routes.push((target, transit));
}
```

Trigger: A DAO message has targets=[A, B, C] and transits=[T1, T2, T3]. All three targets get T1 as their transit info. T2 and T3 are silently dropped.

Bad behavior: Route entries for targets B and C have incorrect transit metadata (wrong path_sequence, path_lifetime, parent). This could cause routing inconsistencies in the federation.

Fix: Either zip targets with transits (targets.into_iter().zip(transits)) or document that only one transit per message is supported.
